\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Intent — retained v0.1 source explanation}

Support reliable association of care information with the intended individual across participating systems.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Boundary — retained v0.1 source explanation}

Harmonia relies on authoritative upstream PAS/\allowbreak{}MPI information for R1/\allowbreak{}R2. Correlation and correction notifications do not establish an autonomous master-patient reconciliation engine.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Harmonia Architectural Relevance — retained v0.1 source explanation}

Identity association is a direct platform concern because clinical records, orders and operational activity need an enduring subject context. Its Core standing does not imply originating master identity authority.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Boundary}

Information administration does not confer authority over the represented person, organisation, service, place, device or clinical activity.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Proposed Placement Rationale}

Responsibility-preserving placement under the human-reviewed BEC hierarchy; the structural assertion remains Proposed.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Reviewed reconciliation provenance}
Reconciliation against the explicit human-reviewed BEC candidate hierarchy. Bounded semantic reconciliation; no unconstrained synthesis \hyperref[evidence:405e9742dcba8b45]{reviewed-bec-hierarchy.json:2}
