\cataloguefield{section}{Capability Overview}

Administer the information and progression of care access, requests, encounters, records and plans across responsible care systems.


\cataloguefield{section}{Definition — Reviewed candidate}

Administer the information and progression of care access, requests, encounters, records and plans across responsible care systems.


\cataloguefield{section}{Boundary}

Information administration does not perform the clinical act, own host booking engines or infer Transfer of Care from referral acceptance.


\cataloguefield{section}{Proposed Placement Rationale}

Responsibility-preserving placement under the human-reviewed BEC hierarchy; the structural assertion remains Proposed.


\cataloguefield{section}{Derivation Provenance}
Inferred from bounded responsibilities and their semantic decomposition. AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task \hyperref[evidence:4bac85accd34ce0b]{business-architecture-metamodel.md:49}; \hyperref[evidence:be61392fefb4bb10]{information-responsibility.md:10}; \hyperref[evidence:27549d51551beae6]{architectural-axioms.md:668}
\cataloguefield{section}{Reviewed reconciliation provenance}
Reconciliation against the explicit human-reviewed BEC candidate hierarchy. Bounded semantic reconciliation; no unconstrained synthesis \hyperref[evidence:405e9742dcba8b45]{reviewed-bec-hierarchy.json:2}
\cataloguefield{section}{Pre-review semantics — historical}

Exact prior assertions are retained as reconciliation evidence, rather than descriptions of the current reviewed capability.


\textbf{Previous definition:} Receive, correlate and communicate the administrative requests, episodes, fulfilment records and documents through which care is arranged and recorded.


\textbf{Previous overview:} Referrals, bookings, encounters, orders and clinical documents have different progression and acknowledgement meanings. Their common ability is to make care administration intelligible across organisations without making those transactions interchangeable.


\textbf{Previous intent:} Keep the requested, accepted, performed and recorded aspects of care administration distinguishable as information crosses systems.


