\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Capability Overview}

Remote \& Virtual Care integrates remotely obtained observations and associates virtual consultations with their patient and episode context. It distinguishes a telemetry contribution from the encounter in which a practitioner may interpret it. The enabling responsibility concerns information continuity across delivery modes, preserving the setting-independent meaning of the Business care capabilities.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Boundary — v0.1 explanation}

Telemetry acquisition is not clinical monitoring judgement or treatment; session association does not establish clinical adequacy.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Harmonia Architectural Relevance}

Remote data and virtual-session context materially extend information continuity across care locations and modes.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Proposed Placement Rationale}

Responsibility-preserving placement under the human-reviewed BEC hierarchy; the structural assertion remains Proposed.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Review Confidence}
Medium; applies to the proposal, not to preserved canonical meaning.
\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Reviewed reconciliation provenance}
Reconciliation against the explicit human-reviewed BEC candidate hierarchy. Bounded semantic reconciliation; no unconstrained synthesis \hyperref[evidence:405e9742dcba8b45]{reviewed-bec-hierarchy.json:2}
